WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:19.099
Brad: Okay, now that we’re safe up here, where do we go?

2
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.862
Tina: Maybe we can swim?

3
00:00:21.863 --> 00:00:24.672
Brad: We can’t swim through soggy land.

4
00:00:24.673 --> 00:00:27.914
Besides, where would we swim to?

5
00:00:27.915 --> 00:00:34.477
Danny: Hey, maybe if we imagine the giants’ world, we will appear there!

6
00:00:34.478 --> 00:00:38.564
Danny: Okay, imagine Ginormous on the count of three.

7
00:00:38.565 --> 00:00:47.043
Danny: Ready? One, two, three!

8
00:00:47.044 --> 00:00:50.734
Brad: I don’t think this is working.

9
00:00:50.735 --> 00:00:55.973
Danny: You’re both imagining Ginormous, right?

10
00:00:55.974 --> 00:01:01.639
Tina: Yes, a world full of giants playing.

11
00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.726
Brad: A giant world without color.

12
00:01:04.727 --> 00:01:08.305
Danny: I don’t think you guys are picturing it right.

13
00:01:08.306 --> 00:01:12.406
Tina: How can we imagine a place we’ve never seen?

14
00:01:12.407 --> 00:01:13.633
Danny: You’re right.

15
00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:17.079
But how else are we going to get out of here!

16
00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:18.648
Danny: Ow!

17
00:01:18.649 --> 00:01:20.598
Brad: What was that?

18
00:01:20.599 --> 00:01:23.963
Danny: That was the sound of my foot on that tree!

19
00:01:23.964 --> 00:01:27.218
Tina: The tree made a funny sound when you kicked it.

20
00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:29.582
Brad: Not funny, hollow.

21
00:01:29.583 --> 00:01:35.394
Danny: But trees aren’t hollow.

22
00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:37.572
Brad: This one is.

23
00:01:37.573 --> 00:01:40.244
Tina: A hollow tree!

24
00:01:40.245 --> 00:01:42.028
Danny: What is it made of?

25
00:01:42.029 --> 00:01:48.280
Brad: It looks like some kind of aluminum, just like a can.

26
00:01:48.281 --> 00:01:52.664
Tina: How is it growing then?

27
00:01:52.665 --> 00:01:55.840
Brad: I don’t think this tree has any roots.

28
00:01:55.841 --> 00:01:59.289
Danny: It’s definitely not a real tree.

29
00:01:59.290 --> 00:02:02.152
It was put here, not planted.

30
00:02:02.153 --> 00:02:05.482
Brad: There might be something interesting underneath it.

31
00:02:05.483 --> 00:02:10.076
Danny: How can we get it up?

32
00:02:10.077 --> 00:02:12.639
Tina: The ground is too wet to dig.

33
00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:16.689
The holes just keep filling up with water.

34
00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:18.412
Brad: Hey, guys?

35
00:02:18.413 --> 00:02:19.954
Danny: What?

36
00:02:19.955 --> 00:02:24.469
Brad: Danny, Tina. Come and stand in a circle around the tree.

37
00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:30.628
Brad: Okay, hold on tight to the tree, and when I say go, [n3@everyone, walk to the right.

38
00:02:30.629 --> 00:02:36.394
Ready? Go!

39
00:02:36.395 --> 00:02:39.330
Danny: Brad! The tree is moving!

40
00:02:39.331 --> 00:02:43.085
Brad: Just as I thought, the tree is screwed into the ground.

41
00:02:43.086 --> 00:02:45.928
Brad: And it’s made of aluminum, so it's pretty light.

42
00:02:45.929 --> 00:02:48.125
Brad: I think we can lift it.

43
00:02:48.126 --> 00:02:50.233
Tina: Way to go, Brad!

44
00:02:50.234 --> 00:03:01.896
Danny: Let’s get this tree out of here!

45
00:03:01.897 --> 00:03:03.895
Brad: What’s down there?

46
00:03:03.896 --> 00:03:07.112
Tina: I don’t know, but it’s dark and wet.

47
00:03:07.113 --> 00:03:10.681
Brad: More water is the last thing we need!

48
00:03:10.682 --> 00:03:15.532
Danny: Well, I think it looks safe.

49
00:03:15.533 --> 00:03:19.391
Tina: I wonder what would happen if we jumped in.

50
00:03:19.392 --> 00:03:21.033
Brad: That’s my point.

51
00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:23.773
We don’t know what might happen!

52
00:03:23.774 --> 00:03:30.630
Danny: Hey! It feels smooth, just like a waterslide.
